  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 343 AM EDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nThe extended period for North and Central Georgia remains largely \nunchanged with this forecast update. Unsettled weather to start with \na return to more seasonable temperatures and lower rain chances as \nwe head into the latter half of the week. The forecast area will be \nsituated in a NW flow regime, supporting the potential for Mesoscale \nConvective Systems (i.e. thunderstorm complexes) to push through \nparts of the TN Valley. While pinpointing the origin and evolution \nof these systems remains uncertain until generally a day or two \nprior, the PoP forecast and severe potential through Wednesday will \nneed to be monitored. At this time, rain and thunderstorm chances \npeak again on Tuesday and Wednesday and lower thereafter due to a \npattern change. Thus, keep an eye on the forecast for those with any \noutdoor plans early to mid-week. \n\nEnsembles continue to favor a cold air damming wedge setting up to \nthe northeast Wednesday night lasting through the end of the work \nweek. Rain changes Thursday heading into the weekend will be much \nmore limited as some drier air works its way into the region. \nAdditionally, forecast high temperatures in the 80s (70s in the \nmountains) and low temperatures in the 50s to 60s) will finally give \nus a taste of fall.",
